Package: oido-dictate
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         python3 (>= 3.9),
         python3-venv,
         python3-numpy,
         python3-tk,
         libportaudio2,
         wtype,
         wl-clipboard,
         curl | wget
Description: On-device speech-to-text dictation (CPU engine)
 A small Wayland "Speak" window that transcribes your voice and types the text
 into whatever window is focused. This base package runs the portable CPU engine
 (statically linked, any arm64) with language-model decoding and adds real
 punctuation and capitalization.
 .
 The model weights are not shipped: they are downloaded on first run from their
 upstream source (see /usr/lib/oido-dictate/fetch-models.sh). Install the
 oido-dictate-gpu add-on on a Raspberry Pi 4 / 400 for the faster GPU engine.

Package: oido-dictate-gpu
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         oido-dictate (= ${binary:Version}),
         libvulkan1,
         mesa-vulkan-drivers
Description: On-device speech-to-text dictation (GPU engine add-on, Pi 4/400)
 Add-on for oido-dictate that enables the hand-written VideoCore VI (V3D 4.2)
 GPU engine, which runs the encoder on the Raspberry Pi 4 / 400 / CM4 GPU and
 leaves the CPU cores free. When present, the Speak window gains the oido-gpu and
 oido-gpu-lm engines and defaults to oido-gpu-lm.
 .
 On any other hardware (e.g. a Pi 5, V3D 7.1) the GPU engine is not used and
 dictation falls back to the CPU engine from oido-dictate.
